WEBVTT

00:07:59.770 --> 00:08:02.046
that guilt is the gift
that keeps on giving.

00:08:02.070 --> 00:08:04.106
FS: Yeah, well, for procrastinators,

00:08:04.130 --> 00:08:05.986
what it gives is more procrastination.

00:08:06.010 --> 00:08:09.076
AG: Ah, so unfair.

00:08:09.100 --> 00:08:11.577
Even if you're not
a chronic procrastinator,

00:08:11.601 --> 00:08:15.223
there are certain types of tasks
that you might have a habit of postponing.

00:08:15.247 --> 00:08:18.285
FS: Might be a procrastinogenic
environment because ...

00:08:18.309 --> 00:08:19.340
(Adam laughs)

00:08:19.364 --> 00:08:21.176
AG: Did you say "procrastinogenic?"

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:23.795
FS: Yes, procrastinogenic.
AG: What a great phrase.

00:08:23.819 --> 00:08:24.819
(Fuschia laughs)

00:08:24.940 --> 00:08:28.094
FS: Well, it's an environment
that can evoke procrastination.

00:08:28.118 --> 00:08:30.786
AG: I am absolutely
using this as an excuse.